        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.257,
            0.886,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": "Humanity has always been fascinated by the shapes of the things around them. In some early cave paintings, the sun is depicted as a circle. In the cave paintings of Gudahandi in Odisha, one sees numerous geometric patterns including triangles, squares, circles, and ovals. These shapes were likely inspired by what humans saw in nature."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.36,
            0.733,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "Can you recognise the origin of the shapes in Fig. 5.1?"
        },
